-- by cubical paths.
--
-- Contents:
-- (1) Exact probability of a sequence of interactions with an environment E: rqm-prob splits identically into
--     classical (diagonal) probability plus quantum interference (rqm-prob-split).
-- (2) Decoherence -> stability theorem (rqm-decoherence-stable): when an environment records the intermediate
--     outcomes orthogonally (ip e_i e_j = 0 for i != j, ip e_i e_i = 1), interference vanishes identically
--     (rqm-interf-zero) and Wigner's probability equals the classical sum of squared amplitudes.
-- (3) Coherent Wigner's-friend theorem (rqm-wigner-coherent): when the environment does not distinguish branches
--     (ip e_i e_j = 1), the exact same rqm-prob computes |sum_i w_i|^2, retaining full quantum interference.
-- (4) Cross-perspective link theorem (rqm-cross-perspective) and warrant transfer from StableFor (rqm-stable-warrants).
-- (5) Timeless relational dynamics (partial observables, no external time t): physical states are exact solutions
--     of H Psi = 0, instantiated on Rovelli's finite spin-clock where clock readings fix system readings.
